---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Ornament from "../components/Ornament.astro";
import { withBase, BRANCHES } from "../lib/site.js";
import { voices, works, hasSpine } from "../lib/portal-data.js";

const vs = [...voices()].sort((a, b) => a.floruit - b.floruit);
const worksByVoice = new Map();
for (const w of works()) {
  for (const v of vs) {
    if ((v.works ?? []).includes(w.id)) {
      if (!worksByVoice.has(v.id)) worksByVoice.set(v.id, []);
      worksByVoice.get(v.id).push(w);
    }
  }
}

const MIN = 500;
const MAX = 1900;
const pos = (y) => ((y - MIN) / (MAX - MIN)) * 100;

const CENTURIES = [];
for (let y = 600; y <= 1900; y += 100) CENTURIES.push(y);
---

<Layout
  title="Timeline"
  description="Five centuries of Arthurian composition, from a monk complaining about Britain in the 540s to a Victorian Poet Laureate in 1885."
  current="/library"
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <span class="rubric">Composition</span>
    <h1>Thirteen centuries, twelve hands</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Not a timeline of the story &mdash; the story has no dates &mdash; but of the writing. This is
      when each of these books was made, and by whom, and it is the single most useful thing to have
      in your head when the versions start contradicting each other.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two facts jump out. Almost everything happens in a burst of about eighty years around 1200.
      And the most famous single scene in the legend, the sword in the stone, is not in the book
      that invented King Arthur &mdash; it arrives three centuries later.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="tl">
    <div class="tl__axis" aria-hidden="true">
      {CENTURIES.map((y) => (
        <span class="tl__tick" style={`left:${pos(y)}%`}>{y}</span>
      ))}
    </div>

    <ol class="tl__rows">
      {
        vs.map((v) => (
          <li class="tl__row" data-branch={v.branch}>
            <div class="tl__label">
              <a href={withBase(`/library/${v.id}/`)}>{v.short ?? v.name}</a>
              <span class="tl__dates">{v.dates}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tl__track">
              <span class="tl__marker" style={`left:${pos(v.floruit)}%`}>
                <span class="tl__dot" />
                <span class="tl__caption">
                  <strong>{v.floruit}</strong>
                  <span>{v.role}</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>

  <Ornament />

  <section class="narrow narrow--flush">
    <span class="rubric">What happened in eighty years</span>
    <h2>The burst around 1200</h2>
    <p>
      Between roughly 1155 and 1235 almost every load-bearing element of the legend is invented or
      fixed. Wace makes the Round Table in 1155. Chrétien invents Arthurian romance, the
      Lancelot&ndash;Guinevere love and the Grail between about 1170 and 1190. Wolfram and Gottfried
      are writing in German around 1205&ndash;1210. The Vulgate cycle is assembled between about
      1215 and 1235, and the <em>Queste</em> lands in the middle of it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everything before that is chronicle, and everything after it &mdash; including Malory, three
      centuries later, and Tennyson, three centuries after him &mdash; is working with material
      that was settled in those eighty years.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="narrow narrow--flush">
    <span class="rubric">The other direction</span>
    <h2>How far the confidence outruns the evidence</h2>
    <p>
      Gildas writes within living memory of Badon and names no Arthur. Nennius, three centuries
      later, credits him with twelve battles and nine hundred and forty men killed by his own hand.
      Geoffrey, three centuries after <em>that</em>, gives him a genealogy from Troy, a court, a
      conquest of Europe and a prophet.
    </p>
    <p>
      The record does not get better as it goes. It gets longer.
      <a href={withBase("/stories/gildas-silence/")}>The silence of Gildas &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .tl { margin: var(--s7) 0; }
  .tl__axis {
    position: relative;
    height: 1.5rem;
    margin-left: 10rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    margin-bottom: var(--s3);
  }
  .tl__tick {
    position: absolute;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-variant-numeric: lining-nums;
  }

  .tl__rows { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .tl__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 10rem 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s3);
    padding: var(--s2) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 60%, transparent);
  }
  .tl__label a { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--branch-ink); }
  .tl__dates { display: block; font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--ink-faint); }

  .tl__track { position: relative; height: 2.6rem; }
  .tl__track::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: 50%;
    height: 1px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--line) 70%, transparent);
  }
  .tl__marker { position: absolute; top: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .tl__dot {
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--branch);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--paper);
  }
  .tl__caption {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    top: 0.75rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .tl__caption strong { display: block; color: var(--branch-ink); font-variant-numeric: lining-nums; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .tl__axis { margin-left: 0; }
    .tl__row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s1); }
    .tl__caption { display: none; }
  }
</style>
